  "title": "Un-Slimy Okra",
  "description": "Roasting the okra with tomatoes keeps it from being slimy, and a dusting of panko adds a touch of crunch to mimic fried okra without the added fat from frying.",
  "authors": [
    "Sarah Garment Stone"
  ],
